 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DfVcdTdNuNK/",
 "title": "Pause Three Seconds Before Answering Job Interview Questions",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "Responding immediately to interview questions can make a candidate seem less certain, despite the urge to answer quickly. Pausing for three full seconds signals that you listened, processed the question, and crafted a deliberate response. This simple pause projects confidence and improves how the interviewer treats you.",
 "key_points": [
  "Responding immediately to interview questions can make you seem less certain of your answer.",
  "Wait a full three seconds before answering a question in an interview.",
  "A three-second pause demonstrates that you heard, received, and thought about what was asked.",
  "Slowing down before responding shows confidence and signals that you have nothing to hide."
 ],
 "content": "Post Text:\nComment “FISHER” for the full episode.\n\nTranscript:\nSpeaker 1: When they ask you an interview question, the faster you respond, the less certain you are of the answer, even though that feels like the opposite. It feels like you have to have a rapid response to make them feel like you know it.\nSpeaker 2: Could you give me an example of that?\nSpeaker 1: Why don't you ask me, \"How was your last week?\"\nSpeaker 2: How was your last week, Jefferson?\nSpeaker 1: It was good. It was good. I mean I, um, you know, it was good. You know, really didn't do too much. Now ask me again.\nSpeaker 2: How was your last week, Jefferson?\nSpeaker 1: It was good. It was hard. You know, we talked about a lot of hard things. I had a really great opportunity to talk about some big lessons with my son. You see how all of a sudden, just those three seconds says, \"I heard what you said. I chose to receive what you said. I thought about what you said, and now I'm thinking about how I respond.\" Wait three seconds. Full three seconds before you respond, and watch how they treat you and how you feel. There's something about the person who's willing to slow down who says, \"I got nothing to hide. I know that I know that I know.\"\n\nText on Screen:\n- Do this in your next job interview\n- The Next Conversation",
 "status": "done",
